<description>&lt;p&gt;The United States has revived a torture indictment against Maduro for ordering torture of rivals and deployed Space Force electromagnetic and electronic warfare systems against Venezuela while pressuring Reliance to refine Venezuelan oil. CIA Director Ratcliffe visited Havana accompanied by a paramilitary operative linked to the operation that killed 32 Cuban soldiers, and he is now shifting focus from Maduro’s capture to Cuba. Opposition leader María Corina Machado has returned to Venezuela after months in exile, prompting nationwide protests demanding elections and her return. The Pentagon has banned DoD personnel from using nonpublic information to bet on U.S. military actions involving Venezuela, and the U.S. Embassy has reopened to full staff, while UCDP recorded 2 battle-related deaths in 2007.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxPNlhmYWRCejlIdUprRExJY0Z2dWJLeFZndzZyVGw2TWQ3eXE5YndISjFvaXo0c0hrbmxzclhIWmw3Q2pJakJzNkYyRjBSUkhLLUZYdHA3X1EyWjUzVDY3bHhYQmpEaFRpX1Bobk5ZR01FX0ViRHNBT3NJWEwxcWE2QTZ6Y1pVclhham5yaEtlWGxCWXpBYmlkbFhJTkR4OHdabFRQOTlPSGVkYjZOVEhuMg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Radio Royal&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE9JV2c0Rkluel9hN3pteUVfdm5BYmhsVUQxWlBRaDdLUkticFFKSWJ6QVVIZ0JnbU9uTi1EUWQyUDF4WEFWYklIc0EtdWlGaHVjckVtcmw3WVU?oc=5&quot;&gt;CubaHeadlines&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuwFBVV95cUxQVkFWLVRPcE1IbzlacmNhS1pZb2FYUFZMcWVqcThHV0JuYURKN3l6dGJrS0NKZUxJNldNV2Q1NUJPZ3dYOHgwOGlUa2VlbmFjbTlEcF9kVkVuNU9IYkhXM1dNQVBYbk91WlRjRjJOY3htSFEwQWtVREg4ZFAzQ0JEQk9CZUtyYjJNcFV0Y2FYZmlSSXJfU1kxbWV4TG4tbFh5YUNFcjl4MzN5UXh6bldzZS11M2o0MFoyVE5B?oc=5&quot;&gt;North Wales Chronicle&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/r